# 01. SOURCE-OF-TRUTH RULE

AEGIS follows one fundamental rule:

> **The domain model owns truth. The interface displays truth.**

A screen must never become the source of truth for an operational entity.

A component must never independently invent the state of an event.

A route must never determine whether an event is resolved.

A mock dataset must never define the actual domain model.

A visual state must never silently become a business state.

The conceptual hierarchy is:

```text
MASTER ARCHITECTURE
        ↓
DOMAIN MODEL
        ↓
GLOBAL STATE MODEL
        ↓
DOMAIN EVENTS
        ↓
USER FLOWS
        ↓
SCREEN SPECIFICATIONS
        ↓
UI COMPONENTS
```

Lower layers may implement higher layers.

Lower layers may not redefine higher layers without an explicit architecture change.

---

# 02. AEGIS DOMAIN PHILOSOPHY

AEGIS is a closed-loop operational system.

Its core domain lifecycle is:

```text
OBSERVE
   ↓
SIGNAL
   ↓
EVENT
   ↓
EVIDENCE
   ↓
ASSESSMENT
   ↓
DECISION
   ↓
RESPONSE
   ↓
VERIFICATION
   ↓
RECOVERY
   ↓
MEMORY
```

This is not merely a workflow.

These are distinct **domain concepts**.

They must not be collapsed into one generic object called "alert" or "incident."

