# 13. OBSERVATION PRINCIPLE

An observation should preserve the difference between:

```text
WHEN IT WAS OBSERVED
```

and:

```text
WHEN AEGIS RECEIVED IT
```

These timestamps are not necessarily identical.

This distinction becomes important for:

- delayed feeds
- offline systems
- synchronization
- historical reconstruction
- data freshness
- event ordering

