# 22. EVENT LIFECYCLE

The canonical lifecycle is:

```text
DETECTED
   ↓
OPEN
   ↓
INVESTIGATING
   ↓
CHARACTERIZING
   ↓
ASSESSED
   ↓
RESPONDING
   ↓
MONITORING
   ↓
RESOLVING
   ↓
CLOSED
   ↓
MEMORIALIZED
```

This is a conceptual lifecycle.

Not every event must pass through every state.

---

# 23. EVENT STATE RULES

### DETECTED

An event has been created from a recognized trigger.

### OPEN

The event is formally active.

### INVESTIGATING

Users are actively gathering or reviewing information.

### CHARACTERIZING

The team is building an understanding of the event.

### ASSESSED

A current assessment exists.

This does **not** mean certainty.

### RESPONDING

A response is actively being coordinated or executed.

### MONITORING

Response or event conditions are being observed.

### RESOLVING

Evidence indicates the event may be moving toward closure.

### CLOSED

The operational event is closed.

### MEMORIALIZED

The event has been incorporated into institutional memory.

---

# 24. EVENT INVARIANT

An Event must never silently transition from:

```text
DETECTED
```

to:

```text
THREAT CONFIRMED
```

without an explicit domain operation and supporting state.

The event lifecycle and threat assessment lifecycle remain separate.

