# 166. DOMAIN COMPLETENESS TEST

The domain model is structurally adequate when the following scenario can be represented without inventing an additional hidden entity:

```text
A new observation arrives.
        ↓
A signal is detected.
        ↓
A human reviews it.
        ↓
An event is created.
        ↓
Evidence is collected.
        ↓
The interpretation changes.
        ↓
An assessment is published.
        ↓
A decision is made.
        ↓
A response is authorized.
        ↓
Actions are executed.
        ↓
The outcome is verified.
        ↓
Recovery occurs.
        ↓
The event closes.
        ↓
Lessons are captured.
```

If the architecture cannot represent any step cleanly, the model is incomplete.

