# 167. GLOBAL STATE COMPLETENESS TEST

The global state architecture is adequate when:

- every screen can read authoritative domain state
- no screen needs to invent domain state
- consequential interactions map to commands
- commands have validation
- successful mutations produce events
- state changes are auditable
- projections update predictably
- stale data is distinguishable
- unknown data is distinguishable
- simulation is isolated
- permission boundaries are enforced
- concurrent changes can be detected
- failed actions cannot masquerade as successful actions

